# Data Science Testing and Validation

## Seeds Make Results Testable
- Pass `random_state=SEED` to every scikit-learn estimator and splitter.
- A test that checks a metric runs twice with the same seed and expects the same number.

## Every Model Beats a Baseline
- Fit a `DummyClassifier` (or `DummyRegressor`) on the same split before any real model.
- Log the baseline score in `experiments/log.md` next to the candidate score.
- A model that does not beat the baseline on the primary metric is not a result.

## Leakage Checks
- Split before any fit: scalers, encoders and imputers are fit on the training fold only (use a `Pipeline`).
- No target-derived feature, and no feature computed with information from after the prediction time.
- No row appears in both train and test (check IDs or a hash of each row).
- Test-set scores are computed once, at the end. Tuning uses validation folds.

## Notebooks Run Top to Bottom
- Restart the kernel and run all cells before handoff.
- Automate it: `pytest --nbval-lax notebooks/` runs each notebook and fails on any error.

## pytest for src/
- Every function in `src/` has at least one test in `tests/test_<module>.py`.
- Tests use the tiny files in `data/fixtures/`, never `data/raw/`.
- Assert on shapes, column names, dtypes and known values, not on printed output.

```python
def test_build_features_keeps_row_count(fixture_df):
    out = build_features(fixture_df)
    assert len(out) == len(fixture_df)
    assert "target" not in out.columns
```

## Done Means
- `pytest tests/` passes
- `pytest --nbval-lax notebooks/` passes
- Baseline and candidate scores are both in `experiments/log.md`
